Remove Duplicates from Sorted Doubly Linked List

Optimal Solution

Approach:
Since the doubly linked list is sorted, duplicate values always appear together.
Traverse the linked list using a pointer temp.
For every node, check if the next node has the same value.
If duplicate nodes are found, keep moving nextNode until a different value is found.
Connect temp->next to this new node.
Also update the prev pointer of the new node to point back to temp.
Continue traversing until the end of the list.

Idea: Keep the first occurrence of every value and remove all the remaining duplicates.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Every node is visited only once.

Space Complexity: O(1)
No extra data structure is used.

Code :

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* removeDuplicates(ListNode* head) {

        ListNode* temp = head;

        while (temp != NULL && temp->next != NULL) {

            // Start checking from the next node
            ListNode* nextNode = temp->next;

            // Skip all duplicate nodes
            while (nextNode != NULL && nextNode->val == temp->val) {
                ListNode* duplicate = nextNode;
                nextNode = nextNode->next;
                delete duplicate;
            }

            // Connect current node with the next different node
            temp->next = nextNode;

            // Update previous pointer
            if (nextNode != NULL) {
                nextNode->prev = temp;
            }

            // Move to the next unique node
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        return head;
    }
};

*
- temp → Current unique node.
- nextNode → Searches for the next different value.
- Skip all duplicate nodes.
- Connect temp with the next unique node.
- Update both next and prev pointers.
- Move temp forward.
